<testgrp id="X39400000R103KC_13_0003" proc-id="RM0550J___00002SV00001">
<testtitle>Inspect Intake Air Flow Meter Sub-assembly</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70201</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Perform an on-vehicle inspection.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Inspect with the vehicle level, in a windless location, and with the engine stopped.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Inspect with the air cleaner assembly installed.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Do not extract exhaust from the exhaust tail pipe with an exhaust duct.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
<test2>
<ptxt>Turn the IG ON and wait for 30 seconds.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display, select [ECU Data Monitor] - [Intake Air Volume] and read the intake air volume.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<title>System selection screen: Powertrain → TCCS → ECU Data Monitor</title>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Item Name</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Intake Air Volume</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Engine stopped</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>30 seconds after turning IG ON</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 0.48 g/sec</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</test2>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Perform a component inspection.</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Remove the intake air flow meter sub-assembly.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A154164J11" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Visually check that there is no foreign matter on the platinum filament (heater) in the passage.</ptxt>
<table>
<title>Text in Illustrations</title>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="0.41in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.72in"/>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>*1</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry>
<ptxt>Platinum filament (heater)</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</test2>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Perform a function check of the intake air flow meter sub-assembly.</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Turn IG ON.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Following the SST (TaSCAN) display screen, select [ECU Data Monitor] - [Intake Air Volume].</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Start the engine.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Check that the intake air volume value changes when racing the engine.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Value changes.</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="X39400000R103KC_13_0004" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="X39400000R103KC_13_0005" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
